			notes: ["Work out the number from the occupant load (Table 3) and the width per person (Table 4), then check it against the travel distance limit (Table 5).", "Count exits floor by floor; the number may never drop as people move along the escape route.", "Lifts, escalators, moving walks, turnstiles and revolving doors never count as exits.", "Part 4 applies to all buildings 15 m and taller, and to special buildings: most non-residential uses with any floor over 500 m², educational and institutional buildings 9 m and taller, all assembly buildings, buildings with over 300 m² of incidental assembly on a floor, and buildings with two or more basements or one basement over 500 m²."],
